# --- Terraform: what must NEVER be committed ---

# Downloaded provider plugins: large, OS-specific. `terraform init` re-fetches them.
.terraform/

# State: a JSON map of your REAL infrastructure. Can contain secrets in plaintext.
# Local state stays on your machine; rung 4 moves it to encrypted S3 (remote state).
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Terraform crash logs.
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Any tfvars that might carry secrets. We'll commit a  *.tfvars.example  instead.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — we DO commit it. It pins
# the exact provider versions so every machine/CI resolves the identical plugins.
